 "dependency_review": "Inspected the intake (Notion idea 3b731704-6eeb-8125-9a72-ca66e87fb8ca, title 'Gemini gems are dead — migrate them into skills!', recording 2026-09-21 15-07-17; the em dash is written as a hyphen in the package title), prep/geminigems.json and its seven stage records, and the full plan set. The three editable projects each carry their own index.html; every local src/href resolves inside its project tree (the whiteboard assets folder is a symbolic link into stage/geminigems_whiteboard that delivery materializes). Generators: geminigems_scene.py (shared scene), the split, cutout and whiteboard generators, the cutout envelope and the proof script, plus the shared code they import via sys.path: pipeline/captions.py, pipeline/pointing_cues.py, pipeline/matting/selection.py, formats/cutout/lib (cutout_core, cutout_depthfield) and formats/whiteboard/lib (whiteboard_build, whiteboard_fix6_core). Media and timing: the raw recording, its full ASR transcript and the whole cuts/geminigems set (master, audio, face plates, EDL, tight transcript) the word-synced captions read. Matting: the matting/geminigems session records, plates, selection and the three shipped v5 layers; the regenerable matting-cache folder is deliberately left out. Config and paperwork: every gen/_* build, spec, geometry, prerender, phone-page, render-control, word-sync and QC record for this Short. Review: Miguel's approval record (final_geminigems.json, approved on the staged videos 2026-09-21 under production v4) and the earlier review records. External runtime dependencies recorded, not vendored: GSAP and Google Fonts fetched at render time, HyperFrames installed globally, ffmpeg for encode. No secrets and no other Short's files."
